      <VERS vnumber="12"> Thou hast caused <gr str="582">men </gr>to <gr str="7392">ride </gr>over our <gr str="7218">heads</gr>; we <gr str="935">went </gr>through <gr str="784">fire </gr>and through <gr str="4325">water</gr>: but thou broughtest us <gr str="3318">out </gr>into a <gr str="7310">wealthy </gr>
        <STYLE css="color:#808080;font-style:italic"> place </STYLE>. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="13"> I will <gr str="935">go </gr>into thy <gr str="1004">house </gr>with burnt <gr str="5930">offerings</gr>: I will <gr str="7999">pay </gr>thee my <gr str="5088">vows</gr>, </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="14">
        <gr str="834">Which </gr>my <gr str="8193">lips </gr>have <gr str="6475">uttered</gr>, and my <gr str="6310">mouth </gr>hath <gr str="1696">spoken</gr>, when I was in <gr str="6862">trouble</gr>. </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="15"> I will <gr str="5927">offer </gr>unto thee burnt <gr str="5930">sacrifices </gr>of <gr str="4220">fatlings</gr>, <gr str="5973">with </gr>the <gr str="7004">incense </gr>of <gr str="352">rams</gr>; I will <gr str="6213">offer </gr>
